senses.gloss:
उदन् + -पानः, -पानम् a small pool or pond near a well, or the well itself;
 K. 50. यावानर्थ उदपाने सर्वतः संप्लुतोदके Bg. 2. 46. ˚मण्डूकः
 (lit.) a frog in a well; (fig.) one who has had no experience of the world
 at large, a man of limited ideas who knows only his own neighbourhood;
 cf. कूपमण्डूक.

उदन् + -पानः, -पानम् a small pool or pond near a well, or the well itself;
 K. 50. यावानर्थ उदपाने सर्वतः संप्लुतोदके Bg. 2. 46. ˚मण्डूकः
 (lit.) a frog in a well; (fig.) one who has had no experience of the world
 at large, a man of limited ideas who knows only his own neighbourhood;
 cf. कूपमण्डूक.

उदन् + -श्वित् n. [उदकन जलेन श्वयति] butter-milk containing
 fifty per cent water (i. e. 2 parts of butter-milk and 1 part of water);
 श्रेयस्तैलं हि पिण्याकाद् घृतं श्रेय उदश्वितः Mb. 12. 167. 35.

उदासीन + .{@-नः@}
—1 A stranger.
—2 A neutral, an indifferent person; अरिमित्रोदासीनव्यवस्था Mu. 5;
 Ms. 7. 158; Y. 1. 345; Bg. 6. 9.
—3 A common acquaintance.

उद्दाम + .{@-मः@}
—1 N. of Yama.
—2 N. of Varuṇa.
